#!/usr/bin/env bash

cat <<-'EOF'

Basic usage:

  asdf list all php
  asdf latest php
  asdf install php <version>
  asdf install php latest
  asdf install php latest:<version>

  php --version
  composer --version

Check the asdf documentation for more instructions on how to install
and manage versions of PHP.

If you use Composer to install a global package that provides
commands (e.g., friendsofphp/php-cs-fixer), you will need to run:

  asdf reshim php

This will make the commands available in your shell.

EOF
